From: Randy Fay <randy.fay@ddev.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:59:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: choose host ports outside the kernel's ephemeral range
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Short Summary (TL;DR)

DDEV now picks the host port for every published container port that leaves it empty, such as the db port or web 80/443, instead of letting Docker or Podman pick one from the kernel's ephemeral range. This removes the `rootlessport listen tcp 127.0.0.1:NNNNN: bind: address already in use` flakes seen in the Podman rootless tests. The router's substitute ports move out of that range too.

## The Issue

When a compose port such as `127.0.0.1::3306` has no host port, the engine picks one from the kernel's ephemeral range (32768-60999 on Linux), which every outgoing connection also draws its source port from. Rootless Podman picks the port when the container is created but only binds it at start, so an unrelated socket can take it in between and the start fails. This hit `TestLastStartedVersionUpdatedByAnyStart`, `TestRouterNotRebuiltWithExtraPorts` and `TestTraefikSharedTLDCerts` in the Podman rootless workflow.

## How This PR Solves The Issue

`fixupComposeYaml` fills in every empty published TCP port, in DDEV's own services and in add-on or custom compose files, with a port from 20000-29999, which is below the ephemeral range on Linux, macOS and Windows. A candidate is checked by binding it, and ports bound by any DDEV container, stopped ones included, are skipped, as are ports reserved by other projects and ports already handed out in this process. An existing container's port is reused, so a running or stopped container isn't recreated just to change port, and the scan starts at a random offset so concurrent starts are unlikely to collide. On a remote Docker host, or when the bind address can't be checked locally, the engine still chooses. Locking concurrent `ddev` processes is left to #5527.

The router's substitute port range moves from 33000-35000 to 30000-32000 for the same reason.

## Manual Testing Instructions

```bash
ddev config --project-type=php
ddev start
docker ps --format '{{.Names}} {{.Ports}}'
# Expect the db and web (80, 443, 8025) host ports in 20000-29999
ddev start
docker ps --format '{{.Names}} {{.ID}} {{.Ports}}'
# Expect the same ports, and the db container not recreated
```

## Automated Testing Overview

`pkg/netutil/netutil_test.go` covers `IsHostPortFree` and `AllocateHostPort`: busy and skipped ports are passed over, and an address that isn't local returns no port. The existing router tests cover the moved substitute range.

## Release/Deployment Notes

Projects whose db, web or Mailpit host port was chosen by the engine get a port in 20000-29999 after their containers are next created. Router substitute ports, shown as "Port 443 is not available, using ... instead", are now 30000-32000. Configured `host_*_port` values are unchanged.

